In this post Blitzschnell describes that they use a regular air filter for airborne contamination control and measure particle counts 1-3 µm and claims this is sufficient for "ISO filling standards". However; ISO 5 requires constant monitoring at particle sizes 0.1, 0.3, 0.5 and 1 µm (https://www.14644.dk/iso-class---particles--size), and in addition to that, unidirectional airflow systems and restricted access barrier systems (https://health.ec.europa.eu/system/files/2022-08/20220825_gmp-an1_en_0.pdf, 4.3, 4.4). This is critical since they are filling open vials with practically zero environmental/airborne contamination control.

