In this post Blitzschnell describes how he cleans the Erlenmeyer flasks; there is no sterilization procedure, just sanitation with benzyl benzoate and isopropyl alcohol. He also references to a TAMC+TYMC report to assure sterility; this is false. TAMC/TYMC is a bioburden test (https://www.nelsonlabs.com/testing/microbial-examination-of-nonsterile-products/), not a sterility test (https://contractlaboratory.com/sterility-testing/). Later, Blitzschnell claims to have acquired a large enough autoclave to fit the Erlenmeyer flask in https://thinksteroids.com/community/threads/blitzschnell-to-fast-secure-reliable-eu-source.134431103/page-181#post-3904191.

